el with one shadow caster and no GI or god rays, 'low' at most 0.5 megapixel with no shadows, bloom or halos; 'auto' is medium on touch screens, high elsewhere.\",\nengine/gfx/quality.ts:52:  /** The most pixels the drawing buffer holds. */\nengine/gfx/quality.ts:54:  /** The most device pixels drawn per CSS pixel. */\nengine/gfx/quality.ts:74:export function qualityBudget(setting: QualitySetting, touch: boolean): QualityBudget {\nengine/dev/governor.ts:2: * @file The performance governor (PLAN.md WP 7.5; the mechanism of `my-3d2dge:src/emberdeep/95-perf.js`, and\nengine/dev/governor.ts:3: * `shardfall:crates/pav_app/src/quality.rs:89-113`'s dynamic scale): while the view setting `quality` is `auto`, it\nengine/dev/governor.ts:4: * moves the page between the quality tiers (engine/gfx/quality.ts) as the frame rate asks, with hysteresis, and on a\nengine/dev/governor.ts:5: * touch screen scales the resolution as well. The page feeds it every drawn frame's real time (`frame(ms)`) and reads\nengine/dev/governor.ts:6: * the budget it affords (`budget(setting, touch)`) where it read `qualityBudget` before (engine/app/drawing.ts).\nengine/dev/governor.ts:13: * screen each bad second also shrinks the drawn pixels' scale by `scale.down` (to `scale.min`), and `scale.calm` good\nengine/dev/governor.ts:14: * seconds in a row grow it by `scale.up` (to 1), shardfall's dynamic resolution.\nengine/dev/governor.ts:16: * A page may give it a memory (`governorMemory`: the tier `auto` settled at for each scene, kept in the page's store):\nengine/dev/governor.ts:22: * setting or the hash (the quality's tiers are view settings' effects). A tier set by hand (`quality` other than\nengine/dev/governor.ts:23: * `auto`) is kept as set, and the governor rests and starts again from `auto`'s tier when `auto` comes back.\nengine/dev/governor.ts:25: * `gfx.governor` is false; the tools' virtual clock gives it even frames, so it never moves under them). Each move is logged once as advice, `GFX_GOVERNOR`, naming\nengine/dev/governor.ts:29: * const governor = createGovernor({ log: { warnOnce: () => true } as never });\nengine/dev/governor.ts:30: * governor.budget('auto', false).tier; // 'high': where auto starts on a desktop\nengine/dev/governor.ts:31: * for (let i = 0; i < 4 * 25; i++) governor.frame(40); // four seconds at 25 frames a second\nengine/dev/governor.ts:32: * governor.budget('auto', false).tier; // 'medium'\nengine/dev/governor.ts:33: * governor.budget('high', false).tier; // 'high': a tier set by hand is kept\nengine/dev/governor.ts:34: * @see engine/dev/governor.test.ts\nengine/dev/governor.ts:40:  qualityBudget,\nengine/dev/governor.ts:45:} from '../gfx/quality';\nengine/dev/governor.ts:50:    template: 'the frame rate moved quality auto to {tier}: {reason}',\nengine/dev/governor.ts:51:    fix: 'nothing to do for play; set quality to a tier (low, medium, high) to hold one, or gfx.governor to false',\nengine/dev/governor.ts:52:    doc: 'Advice from the performance governor (engine/dev/governor.ts) when it moves the `auto` quality a tier.',\nengine/dev/governor.ts:58:  'gfx.governor': {\nengine/dev/governor.ts:63:      'Whether the performance governor may move quality auto between its tiers as the frame rate asks (engine/dev/governor.ts); a tier set by hand is kept either way.',\nengine/dev/governor.ts:68:/** The governor's numbers (see the file comment): seconds, milliseconds a frame, and the scale's steps. */\nengine/dev/governor.ts:77:  scale: { down: 0.88, up: 1.06, min: 0.6, calm: 4 },\nengine/dev/governor.ts:83:/** What the governor holds now. */\nengine/dev/governor.ts:85:  /** The tier `auto` stands at, or null while `quality` is set by hand. */\nengine/dev/governor.ts:87:  /** The drawn pixels' scale on a touch screen (1 elsewhere). */\nengine/dev/governor.ts:88:  scale: number;\nengine/dev/governor.ts:100:/** The governor (see the file comment). */\nengine/dev/governor.ts:118:/** The key of a page's store under which `governorMemory` keeps each scene's tier. */\nengine/dev/governor.ts:119:export const GOVERNOR_STORE_KEY = 'gfx.governor';\nengine/dev/governor.ts:122:export function governorMemory(\nengine/dev/governor.ts:140:/** Makes a governor; `log` takes its advice (the shared log by default), `memory` keeps where `auto` settled. */\nengine/dev/governor.ts:143:  const s = { tier: null as QualityTier | null, start: 'high' as QualityTier, scale: 1, scaleCalm: 0, calm: GOVERNOR.calmStart as number, bad: 0, good: 0, seconds: 0, moves: 0, frozen: false, promoted: -Infinity }; // prettier-ignore\nengine/dev/governor.ts:164:      if (slow) [s.scale, s.scaleCalm] = [Math.max(GOVERNOR.scale.min, s.scale * GOVERNOR.scale.down), 0];\nengine/dev/governor.ts:165:      else if (fast && ++s.scaleCalm >= GOVERNOR.scale.calm)\nengine/dev/governor.ts:166:        [s.scale, s.scaleCalm] = [Math.min(1, s.scale * GOVERNOR.scale.up), 0]; // prettier-ignore\nengine/dev/governor.ts:167:      else if (!fast) s.scaleCalm = 0;\nengine/dev/governor.ts:189:        [s.tier, s.scale, ms, frames] = [null, 1, 0, 0]; // at rest: `auto` starts again from its own tier\nengine/dev/governor.ts:190:        return qualityBudget(setting, onTouch);\nengine/dev/governor.ts:194:      const budget = qualityBudget(s.tier, onTouch);\nengine/dev/governor.ts:195:      if (!onTouch || s.scale === 1) return budget;\nengine/dev/governor.ts:198:        maxPixels: budget.maxPixels === null ? null : budget.maxPixels * s.scale * s.scale,\nengine/dev/governor.ts:199:        maxPixelRatio: budget.maxPixelRatio === null ? null : budget.maxPixelRatio * s.scale,\nengine/dev/governor.ts:206:      const { tier, scale, calm, bad, good, seconds, moves, frozen } = s;\nengine/dev/governor.ts:207:      return { tier, scale, calm, bad, good, seconds, moves, frozen };\nengine/gfx/resolution.ts:82:  pixelRatio: number;\nengine/gfx/resolution.ts:103:/** The drawing buffer `mode` gives a canvas of `css` size at `devicePixelRatio`, within `cap` (none by default). */\nengine/gfx/resolution.ts:104:export function fitResolution(css: Size, devicePixelRatio: number, mode: ResolutionMode, cap: PixelCap = {}): Fit {\nengine/gfx/resolution.ts:106:  const pixelRatio = Math.min(MAX_PIXEL_RATIO, ratioCap, devicePixelRatio > 0 ? devicePixelRatio : 1);\nengine/gfx/resolution.ts:108:    width: Math.max(1, Math.round(css.width * pixelRatio)),\nengine/gfx/resolution.ts:109:    height: Math.max(1, Math.round(css.height * pixelRatio)),\nengine/gfx/resolution.ts:128:    pixelRatio,\nengine/gfx/resolution.ts:162:  /** The device pixel ratio now: `window.devicePixelRatio` by default. */\nengine/gfx/resolution.ts:163:  pixelRatio?: () => number;\nengine/gfx/resolution.ts:170:  const pixelRatio = options.pixelRatio ?? (() => globalThis.devicePixelRatio ?? 1);\nengine/gfx/resolution.ts:195:      const ratio = pixelRatio();\nengine/ui/widgets.ts:70:.ui-heart { color: #3a1826; }\nengine/ui/widgets.ts:71:.ui-heart[data-fill='full'] { color: #e8384a; }\nengine/ui/widgets.ts:72:.ui-heart[data-fill='half'] { color: transparent; background: linear-gradient(90deg, #e8384a 50%, #3a1826 50%);\nengine/ui/widgets.ts:75:  border: 2px solid #e8e4ff; border-radius: 6px; box-shadow: 3px 3px 0 #05040a; color: #ffffff; }\nengine/ui/widgets.ts:77:.ui-box-title, .ui-menu-title, .ui-dialog-name { color: #ffd36a; }\nengine/ui/widgets.ts:88:  color: #ffd36a; }\nengine/ui/widgets.ts:93:.ui-choice[data-value='selected'], .ui-menu-item[data-value='selected'] { color: #ffd36a;\nengine/ui/widgets.ts:97:.ui-menu-item[data-value='disabled'] { color: #6a6488; cursor: default; }\nengine/ui/overlay.ts:128:  font: 600 16px/1.2 system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif; color: #f0e3c6;\nengine/ui/overlay.ts:140:  font-size: calc(var(--ui-scale, 1) * 1.25em); font-weight: 800; line-height: 1; color: #fff2c4;\nengine/ui/overlay.ts:217:  const lines = new Map<string, { el: HTMLElement; color: string }>();\nengine/ui/overlay.ts:272:        line = { el: div(doc, 'ui-hud'), co