{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_103","type":"agent_message","text":"The headless suite now passes all 18 tests. It covers five input patterns across ten seeds per activity, capture/restore, and complete five-day playthroughs on three seeds. Those full playthroughs caught a dive path that crossed the cliff terrain; the corrected arc now reaches the ending safely. Next are browser controls, Hub multiplayer, and viewport checks.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_104","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> ../PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Current milestone: first full model pass\n- \"'`npx vitest run labs/game/scenes/game.test.ts --maxWorkers=1`: 18/18 PASS, 27.45 s. Covers 10 seeds × 5 input patterns per activity, all poses, exact capture/restore, full five-day story to credits on 3 seeds.\n- Chromium WebGPU boots with zero engine errors; title screenshot inspected at 1920×1080 (`out/game/title.png`). Full-resolution presentation selected explicitly (engine otherwise defaults to 330 lines).\n- Root HTML is currently built but stale relative to latest edits. Rebuild with `node labs/game/tools/onefile.mjs` from dev root.\n- Need finish: browser suite (keyboard/mouse/pad, saves, touch, dev, attract), real Hub harness 2/3/4 players + host-leave, viewport matrix screenshots including WebKit unsupported page, audio numerical tests, golden replays, npm check/test, final reports and exit-interview JSON.\n- All ongoing exec sessions finish on their own; no server has been started yet. Headless Playwright processes are closed by their Python scripts.\n- Test assets moved to dev `.cache/hub/` to keep upstream harness files pristine and out of game lint. `session-client.txt` is pristine; trimmed SHA-256 is plan'\"'s \"'`529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a` (whole-file SHA includes final LF and differs).\n- `labs/game/ui/about-data.ts` is canonical report data; feedback counts currently unknown, update before final bundle. Final exit interview must be exported from it.\n- 212 original short dialogue/notice/result lines now in `ui/lines/cast.ts`, connected to cast and plaque interactions.\n\n## Distinct defects caught so far (track final tally from this list)\n1. Negative rhythm chart index for delayed bots (critical crash) — fixed.\n2. Rewards decayed after course/tray completion — activities now finish on completion.\n3. Dive bot release missed swinging gauge — fixed.\n4. Referenced nonexistent built-in sand texture (critical startup) — original flat sand material used.\n5. Menu action map omitted default movement actions (critical startup) — fixed.\n6. Rebuilding terrain for every height query slowed setup — cache immutable ground data.\n7. Dive arc crossed terrain (critical story blocker) — arc corrected, full story passes.\n8. Paddle used raw target input while balance sway accumulated topples — now uses CoB and a sustained alternating-foot boost.\n9. Engine pixel resolution default did not match intended art — explicitly full resolution.\n10. Engine overlay typography coloured activity heading cream — explicit game typography reset.\n11. Attract timer elapsed during engine warm-up — reset when game is ready.\n12. Presentation guides wrote phase/pose data — made guide readers pure.\n13. Attract exit input could also choose a menu item — consumed that first input.\n- Critical count so far: 4 (items 1,4,5,7).\n\n## Recent edits to verify\n- Appearance choice now changes puppet body; initial 3 colours, further colours unlock with pebbles.\n- Hub seat-coloured puppet bodies, remote names in Group HUD.\n- Expert variants toggle by left/right on Noticeboard after 10 pebbles.\n- Cairo/cairn pebbles, creeping plaques, Tare follows and hops; finale spawns 12 visible guests.\n- Font-size check should account for SVG text scaling, or exclude decorative SVG labels; disc label now 10 viewBox px.\n- Touch attract still needs a persistent Settings button/message; unsupported browser Back currently can return normal title and should be kept friendly.\n- App currently ~400 lines; keep it under 400 by extracting runtime helpers as needed. No engine files have been edited.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_104","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> ../PROGRESS.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Current milestone: first full model pass\n- \"'`npx vitest run labs/game/scenes/game.test.ts --maxWorkers=1`: 18/18 PASS, 27.45 s. Covers 10 seeds × 5 input patterns per activity, all poses, exact capture/restore, full five-day story to credits on 3 seeds.\n- Chromium WebGPU boots with zero engine errors; title screenshot inspected at 1920×1080 (`out/game/title.png`). Full-resolution presentation selected explicitly (engine otherwise defaults to 330 lines).\n- Root HTML is currently built but stale relative to latest edits. Rebuild with `node labs/game/tools/onefile.mjs` from dev root.\n- Need finish: browser suite (keyboard/mouse/pad, saves, touch, dev, attract), real Hub harness 2/3/4 players + host-leave, viewport matrix screenshots including WebKit unsupported page, audio numerical tests, golden replays, npm check/test, final reports and exit-interview JSON.\n- All ongoing exec sessions finish on their own; no server has been started yet. Headless Playwright processes are closed by their Python scripts.\n- Test assets moved to dev `.cache/hub/` to keep upstream harness files pristine and out of game lint. `session-client.txt` is pristine; trimmed SHA-256 is plan'\"'s \"'`529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a` (whole-file SHA includes final LF and differs).\n- `labs/game/ui/about-data.ts` is canonical report data; feedback counts currently unknown, update before final bundle. Final exit interview must be exported from it.\n- 212 original short dialogue/notice/result lines now in `ui/lines/cast.ts`, connected to cast and plaque interactions.\n\n## Distinct defects caught so far (track final tally from this list)\n1. Negative rhythm chart index for delayed bots (critical crash) — fixed.\n2. Rewards decayed after course/tray completion — activities now finish on completion.\n3. Dive bot release missed swinging gauge — fixed.\n4. Referenced nonexistent built-in sand texture (critical startup) — original flat sand material used.\n5. Menu action map omitted default movement actions (critical startup) — fixed.\n6. Rebuilding terrain for every height query slowed setup — cache immutable ground data.\n7. Dive arc crossed terrain (critical story blocker) — arc corrected, full story passes.\n8. Paddle used raw target input while balance sway accumulated topples — now uses CoB and a sustained alternating-foot boost.\n9. Engine pixel resolution default did not match intended art — explicitly full resolution.\n10. Engine overlay typography coloured activity heading cream — explicit game typography reset.\n11. Attract timer elapsed during engine warm-up — reset when game is ready.\n12. Presentation guides wrote phase/pose data — made guide readers pure.\n13. Attract exit input could also choose a menu item — consumed that first input.\n- Critical count so far: 4 (items 1,4,5,7).\n\n## Recent edits to verify\n- Appearance choice now changes puppet body; initial 3 colours, further colours unlock with pebbles.\n- Hub seat-coloured puppet bodies, remote names in Group HUD.\n- Expert variants toggle by left/right on Noticeboard after 10 pebbles.\n- Cairo/cairn pebbles, creeping plaques, Tare follows and hops; finale spawns 12 visible guests.\n- Font-size check should account for SVG text scaling, or exclude decorative SVG labels; disc label now 10 viewBox px.\n- Touch attract still needs a persistent Settings button/message; unsupported browser Back currently can return normal title and should be kept friendly.\n- App currently ~400 lines; keep it under 400 by extracting runtime helpers as needed. No engine files have been edited.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_105","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('labs/game/ui/screens/programme.ts');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"a.show('board',page)\\\",\\\"a.show('board',0)\\\",1);p.write_text(s)\np=Path('labs/game/app.ts');s=p.read_text();a=s.index(\\\"    Object.defineProperty(window, '__game'\\\");b=s.index('    requestAnimationFrame(this.uiLoop);',a);block=s[a:b]\nruntime=Path('labs/game/ui/runtime.ts');runtime.write_text('/** @file Read-only browser inspection handle and persistent touch-only demo guard. */\\\\nimport type {GameApp} from \\\\'../app\\\\';\\\\nimport {glyph} from \\\\'./glyphs\\\\';\\\\nexport function publishState(app:GameApp):void{\\\\n'+block.replace('this.','app.')+'}\\\\n'+'''export function updateBanner(app:GameApp):void{\n const banner=app.attract?\"'`<div class=\"demo-pill\">Wobble Fit <b>DEMO</b> ${glyph('\"'accept',app.ui.device,app.options.xbox)} Press any button</div>\"'${app.touchOnly?'\"'<div class=\\\"touch-guard\\\">Controller or keyboard required<button type=\\\"button\\\" data-touch-settings>Settings</button></div>':''}\"'`:'\"'';\n if(app.ui.banner.innerHTML===banner)return;\n app.ui.banner.innerHTML=banner;\n app.ui.banner.querySelector('[data-touch-settings]')?.addEventListener('click',()=>{app.exitAttract();app.show('settings');});\n}\n''')\ns=s[:a]+'    publishState(this);\\\\n'+s[b:];s=s.replace(\\\"import { glyph, safe } from './ui/glyphs';\\\", \\\"import { safe } from './ui/glyphs';\\\\nimport {publishState,updateBanner} from './ui/runtime';\\\")\na=s.index('    const banner = this.attract');b=s.index(\\\"    if (this.engine && this.flow?.mode\\\",a);s=s[:a]+'    updateBanner(this);\\\\n'+s[b:];s=s.replace('  private exitAttract(): void', '  exitAttract(): void');s=s.replace('  hubNames: string[]=[];', '  noGpu=false;\\\\n  hubNames: string[]=[];');s=s.replace('title, arrival, pause, tools, controls, group', 'title, arrival, pause, tools, controls, group, unsupported');s=s.replace('    this.page = page;', \\\"    if(screen==='title' && this.noGpu){unsupported(this);return;}\\\\n    this.page = page;\\\");p.write_text(s)\np=Path('labs/game/ui/screens/front.ts');s=p.read_text()+'''\\\\nexport function unsupported(a:ScreenApp):void{\n a.ui.menu('unsupported','A SMALL TECHNICAL MATTER','A different browser.<br>The same little island.','This game needs a browser with WebGPU, such as current Chrome or Edge.',[{id:'settings',label:'Settings',action:()=>a.show('settings')},{id:'about',label:'About the retreat',action:()=>a.show('about')}],{extra:a.touchOnly?'<p class=\\\"touch-required\\\">Controller or keyboard required</p>':''});\n a.ui.root.classList.add('no-gpu');\n a.ui.back=()=>{};\n}\n''';p.write_text(s)\np=Path('labs/game/main.ts');s=p.read_text();a=s.index(\\\"  app.ui.menu('unsupported'\\\") if \\\"  app.ui.menu('unsupported'\\\" in s else s.index('  app.ui.menu(\\\\n');b=s.index('  if (session.info)',a);s=s[:a]+\\\"  app.noGpu=true;app.show('title');\\\\n\\\"+s[b:];p.write_text(s)\nPY\ncat >> labs/game/ui/theme.css <<'EOF'\n.touch-guard{position:fixed;left:6vw;right:6vw;bottom:5vh;background:#f6f3e8ed;border-radius:1.2vh;padding:1.5vh 4vw;display:flex;gap:4vw;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;font-size:2.2vh;pointer-events:auto}.touch-guard button{border:1px solid #9eaf91;background:#dce5ce;padding:1vh 4vw;border-radius:1vh;color:#365441}\nEOF\nnpx tsc -b tsconfig.check.json --pretty false\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
