{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_109","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n \\\"GFX.*GPU|NO.*GPU|adapter\\\" engine/gfx/renderer.ts | head -40; rg -n 'async function|body\\\\[|data-complete|check\\\\(' .cache/hub/harness.html | tail -25; ls /home/micha/.cache/ms-playwright | head -12; tail -6 out/game/browser.log\"","aggregated_output":"3: * `createRenderer` asks for a WebGPU adapter before anything else and refuses to start without one (`GFX_NO_WEBGPU`,\n4: * naming the fix). It creates the device itself, with every adapter feature and the adapter's limits\n6: * `WebGPURenderer`, so three.js never requests an adapter of its own and its WebGL 2 fallback has nothing to fall back\n7: * from; `await renderer.init()` follows, then the backend assertion. It then reports the GPU (`info`: adapter,\n9: * routes WebGPU's errors to the log: an uncaptured validation or memory error as `GFX_GPU_ERROR`, a lost device as\n26: * fix, and nothing is drawn, configured or allocated on the GPU before the adapter check passes. Rendering settings\n30: * const refused = await requestWebGPU(undefined).catch((error: GfxError) => error.code); // 'GFX_NO_WEBGPU' in Node\n48:  GFX_NO_WEBGPU: {\n51:    doc: 'Raised at startup, before anything touches the GPU, when the browser has no `navigator.gpu`, gives no adapter or device, or three.js starts another backend than WebGPU. WebGPU is the only renderer: there is no WebGL fallback (PLAN.md §6.7), so nothing starts, and a page shows this message with its fix.',\n57:  GFX_GPU_ERROR: {\n105:  /** The adapter's identity (on this platform: vendor `google`, architecture `swiftshader`, a fallback adapter). */\n106:  adapter: GfxCaps['adapter'];\n107:  /** The adapter's features, sorted; the device has every one of them. */\n109:  /** The device's limits, by name: the adapter's own, unless `GFX_DEFAULT_LIMITS` said otherwise. */\n213: * Asks `gpu` (by default the browser's `navigator.gpu`) for an adapter; rejects with `GfxError` `GFX_NO_WEBGPU` when\n214: * there is no WebGPU or no adapter. Nothing is created on the GPU.\n217:  if (!gpu) throw new GfxError('GFX_NO_WEBGPU', { reason: 'this browser has no navigator.gpu' });\n218:  let adapter: GPUAdapter | null;\n220:    adapter = await gpu.requestAdapter();\n222:    throw new GfxError('GFX_NO_WEBGPU', { reason: `navigator.gpu.requestAdapter() failed (${String(error)})` });\n224:  if (!adapter) throw new GfxError('GFX_NO_WEBGPU', { reason: 'navigator.gpu.requestAdapter() gave no adapter' });\n225:  return adapter;\n237:    log.error('GFX_GPU_ERROR', { kind: error.constructor.name, message: error.message });\n247: * Starts three.js's `WebGPURenderer` on `canvas`, on WebGPU only: the adapter check, a device with every feature and\n248: * limit the adapter offers, `await renderer.init()`, the backend assertion, then the report, the feature registry and\n249: * the error routes. Rejects with `GfxError` `GFX_NO_WEBGPU` at the first step that fails. Draw with `frame(view)`.\n254:  const adapter = await requestWebGPU();\n257:    device = await requestDevice(adapter, { log });\n259:    throw new GfxError('GFX_NO_WEBGPU', { reason: `the adapter gave no device (${String(error)})` });\n262:  const caps = readCaps(adapter, device);\n270:    throw new GfxError('GFX_NO_WEBGPU', { reason: 'three.js started another backend than WebGPU' });\n278:    adapter: caps.adapter,\n384:async function until(test, ms) {\n404:async function conformance() {\n416:      check('game named', false, 'pass ?game=<path> of a page on this site');\n421:    check('head metas', m && m.session === '1' && modeOf(m.mode), m ? `hub:session=${m.session} mode=${m.mode}` : 'could not fetch the page');\n424:    check('hub:session-players is a range within 1–4', seats.length >= 1 && seats.length <= 2 && least >= 1 && least <= most && most <= 4, `hub:session-players=${m?.players}`);\n425:    if (m?.minutes != null) check('hub:session-minutes, when given, is a number', Number(m.minutes) > 0, `hub:session-minutes=${m.minutes}`);\n430:    check('every copy says hello', helloed, copies().filter((p) => !p.hello).map((p) => p.key).join(', '));\n433:    check('hello names protocol 1 and the mode', caps.every((c) => c.v === 1 && modeOf(c.mode) === state.coordinator.mode), JSON.stringify(caps[0]));\n434:    check('hello seats cover this player count', caps.every((c) => Array.isArray(c.seats) && c.seats[0] <= Math.max(2, n) && c.seats[1] >= n), JSON.stringify(caps[0]?.seats));\n436:      check('frames reachable for synthetic input', false, 'serve the game from the same origin as this harness');\n442:    check('ready without a key press (the card asks the players)', loaded, copies().filter((p) => !p.ready).map((p) => p.key).join(', '));\n449:      check('its own card: Enter answers Ready', sent && answered, players.filter((c) => !state.answers.ready.has(c.key)).map((c) => `${c.key}${c.cardSent ? '' : ' (no card yet)'}`).join(', '));\n453:    check('the round starts when the card ends', started && copies().every((p) => p.ready), copies().filter((p) => !p.ready).map((p) => p.key).join(', ') || state.status?.phase);\n474:      check(`${mode}: Math.random is seeded, the same on every copy`, seeded, state.cells.map((c) => `${c.key}: client ${c.frame.contentWindow?.AIHub?.version ?? '?'} seeded ${c.frame.contentWindow?.AIHub?.seeded}`).join('; '));\n483:        check('parallel: no game traffic', state.cells.every((c) => c.bridge.stats.sent === 0),\n486:        check('ghost: every copy sends its player', remaining.every((c) => c.bridge.stats.sent > 0) || n === 1,\n489:      if (!legacyRace) check(`${mode}: every copy reports its progress`, remaining.every((c) => c.progress.length > 0 || state.status?.players.find((p) => p.key === c.key)?.result),\n492:      check('game traffic flows both ways', remaining.every((c) => c.bridge.stats.sent > 0 && c.bridge.stats.received > 0) || n === 1,\n502:      check('a copy with no player of its own runs the world (as a server would)', ended && record.status === 'played' && record.hostId === serverCell.bridge.me && serverCell.bridge.stats.sent > 0,\n506:      check('host leaving voids the round', ended && record.status === 'void' && record.endReason === 'host-left', record ? `${record.status} (${record.reason})` : 'no end');\n508:      check('the round ends with a valid result', ended && record.status === 'played', record ? `${record.status} (${record.reason})` : 'no end within the grace period');\n511:    check('every remaining copy is told the round ended', remaining.every((c) => c.bridge.ended), remaining.filter((c) => !c.bridge.ended).map((c) => c.key).join(', '));\n513:    check('no protocol problems', issues.length === 0, issues.map((i) => `${i.key}: ${i.problem}`).join('; '));\n521:    check('no errors, dialogs, popups or sockets', violations.length === 0, violations.slice(0, 6).join('; '));\n523:    check('harness ran', false, String(error?.stack || error));\nchromium-1243\nchromium_headless_shell-1243\nffmpeg-1011\nfirefox-1543\nwebkit-2359\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
