\nstep: 300 steps, 2 golden hashes, final 2533e2b6d84e1c22: Node ×2, Chromium ×2, all match\ntilt: 300 steps, 2 golden hashes, final 3472a5c14c1e8d4f: Node ×2, Chromium ×2, all match\nreport: out/replay/labs-game-replays/report.json\ntotal 5044\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha     514 Nov  4 23:41 browser.log\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha     530 Nov  4 23:41 browser-report.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   21604 Nov  4 23:41 firefox-phone.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha      52 Nov  4 23:41 check.log\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha      74 Nov  4 23:41 format-audio.log\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   53745 Nov  4 23:41 webkit-phone.png\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha    1429 Nov  4 23:39 replays.log\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_118","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > labs/game/README.md <<'EOF'\n# Wobble Fit\n\nA complete five-day residency at Little Fulcrum, a wellness island balanced on one rock. Lean is your centre of balance; the same input becomes a held pose, a slackline correction, a paddle stroke, a sand tray, and eventually the island itself. The game has thirteen activities, a walkable island, daily Wobble Ages, pebbles, growing cairn, 212 short remarks, a storm finale, free practice and a four-seat group round.\n\n## Play and share\n\nOpen the root deliverable \"'`Wobble-Fit-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261104-224022.html` directly in a WebGPU-capable Chrome or Edge. Everything, including the unmodified AI Hub client, is inlined; no download is needed. WebKit and Firefox receive the explicit WebGPU requirement screen. WebKit iPhone emulation is the available Safari stand-in, not real iOS.\n\nUse a standard-mapped controller: left stick to lean/walk, triggers or shoulders for the two feet, both for breathing, Cross to select, Options to pause, Triangle for the Programme. PlayStation glyphs are the default; Settings can use Xbox glyphs. Keyboard: WASD/arrows, Q/E feet, Space both, Enter/E use, Tab programme, Escape pause. A captured mouse leans and its buttons act as feet; the garden uses its visible position. Hover moves menu focus. Touch-only screens show the required-controller notice and Settings; attract still runs.\n\nThe Programme provides instant travel, so exploration is optional. Completing an activity at any rank counts. Finish today'\"'s programme and sleep. After the storm, the last check leads to credits and all activities stay available. Group Class fills empty mats with CPU guests (optional). In AI Hub every copy owns its round and draws neighbouring ghost guests; host departure does not interrupt the class.\n\n## Build and verification\n\nFrom this development workspace:\n\n- \"'`node labs/game/tools/onefile.mjs` builds the required root HTML.\n- `node labs/game/tools/verify.mjs` runs the complete verification, printing failures and one count line; `--quick` selects the Node stages.\n- `npm run check` checks types, lint, format, assets and all 2,135 read-only engine files.\n- `npm test -- --maxWorkers=1` runs activity, complete-story, restoration and numerical audio tests.\n- `node x replay labs/game/replays --browser sim --runs 2` checks the original-content goldens in Node and Chromium. Set CHROMIUM_PATH to this machine'\"'s installed headless shell as PLAN.md specifies.\n\nTests and screenshots live under this workspace's \"'`out/` directory, as TASK.md requires all generated files to remain inside our own folder. The viewport tool'\"'s usual temporary output directory was overridden for that reason. The checks use ephemeral loopback servers only, close their own browsers and servers, and never touch another worker's processes. The test harness is upstream data kept in \"'`.cache/hub/`; it is not shipped or modified.\n\n## Implementation calls\n\n- Full read-only my-3dge workspace pinned to the plan-tested e7a124394afe087a40c36e2662a5c4ca2b39a663. No engine or configuration patches, no new dependency, no binary game asset, no external publication.\n- The random title draw selected candidate 3 (zero-based) from 50 via Python `secrets.randbelow`. The root `title-selection.json` records the actual draw.\n- One deterministic island scene owns all activities; a smaller separate pavilion scene meets the Hub boot deadline. Every playable character has `player:false` and one pilot writes its intents.\n- Activities share one 60 Hz balance and breathing model but retain independent rules, integrators, rhythm windows, course counters and scoring. The sandbox, bot and live sliders use recorded scene actions/settings.\n- The single HTML is built with Vite and injects the untouched session client from text. The SHA-256 of its banner through last non-whitespace character matches the protocol'\"'s 1.4.0 client hash.\n- New poses are hand-authored key strips on the native humanoid clip layer. Mesh2Motion supplies only the reference rest skeleton. No licensed STYLE100 or CMU clips were copied.\n- The sand tray has a large readable SVG instrument over its 3D table. Marble motion, ridges, cups and captures remain deterministic sim state.\n- Full resolution and high quality are explicit, because performance is outside this brief and the engine's automatic resolution otherwise chooses 330 lines. The game keeps its own typography inside the engine overlay.\n- The roughly 45-minute residency uses bounded activities and optional travel. Every activity finishes with idle input. The test bot accelerates sim progression; it never creates a separate set of gameplay rules.\n- Data tables in \"'`scenes/data/` hold days, poses, charts, trays and lures. Original lines are `ui/lines/cast.ts`. Final source information and interview answers have one canonical home in `ui/about-data.ts`.\n- Physical controllers, real iOS Safari, a TV and human audio listening are unavailable. Tests substitute standard-mapped pad data, WebKit device profiles, 1920×1080 screenshots and numerical PCM levels.\n\nThe running implementation and test defect tally are recorded in the root `PROGRESS.md`. The exit interview and in-game About pages disclose the exact final test results and limitations.\nEOF\ncat > README.md <<'\"'EOF'\n# Wobble Fit\n\nThe full development workspace for the self-contained Little Fulcrum balance game. Start with [the game README](labs/game/README.md). The engine is pinned and read-only; its exact provenance is in engine-lock.json and ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md.\n\nBuild: \"'`node labs/game/tools/onefile.mjs`. Verify: `node labs/game/tools/verify.mjs`.\nEOF\ncat > ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md <<'\"'EOF'\n# Engine feedback — Wobble Fit\n\nEngine: my-3dge e7a124394afe087a40c36e2662a5c4ca2b39a663. The game uses the full generated workspace.\n\n## What worked\n\nThe deterministic world, recorded scene actions, headless inspector, capture/restore and procedural puppet/prop APIs fit this game well. Original pose strips and additive lean layers can be scrubbed directly from hashed sim data. A separate small round scene allows the same mechanics to work in a Hub session without building the island there.\n\n## Integration findings\n\n- \"'`getTerrain` explicitly returns a fresh grid. Initially the game'\"'s height helper called it for every query, making setup needlessly slow. The game now caches one immutable terrain and calls \"'`terrainHeight` on it. A cached-terrain example would make this easier to discover.\n- A custom action map inherits movement names, so a menu map with `actions:{}` is rejected by CORE_BAD_SPEC. The game supplies the standard walk actions and keeps `lock:false`; modal still prevents gameplay input.\n- The native texture library has no sand entry. A guessed texture:sand caused a fail-fast CORE_BAD_SPEC. The game uses an original plain sand material. The public registry'\"'s error listed all valid choices and made the fix immediate.\n- Props use \"'`{at,yaw}`, not `{position}`. `addBox` creates a dynamic prop and takes size separately; the small session floor instead uses the public physics `addBody` with a fixed collider. Type checking caught both wrong assumptions.\n- The default automatic resolution is 330 lines when a custom look omits resolution. It made a clean retreat look pixelated. The page explicitly requests `gfx.resolution=full`, `quality=high`, and disables the automatic governor.\n- HTML appended below engine.ui.root inherits the native overlay'\"'s 600-weight text and cream colour. The game resets these on its own shell and HUD.\n- Source-side JSON rest imports trigger TS6307 in this generated composite project unless listed explicitly. Without changing the engine-owned tsconfig, the game keeps the reference rest as a readable TypeScript export; the original JSON remains beside it.\n- Scrubbed clips are played at spawn or during the first step, never in setup. Multiple additive slots are scrubbed directly. Full body changes replace older layers through the native clip stack.\n- A browser's initial \"'`__engine.ready` can precede the game'\"'s own attachment by a frame. Startup input is queued and the attract timer is reset on attachment, so it cannot begin before the title has had its full idle interval.\n- Hub query parameters are stripped before createEngine. Harness checks additionally verify actual engine readiness and a ghost entity; protocol success alone would conceal a dead game.\n\n## Most valuable improvement\n\nA documented small example combining recorded scene actions, a custom camera, a menu action map and a single-file build would remove several interface guesses. A public setting getter on the inspector would also simplify live tuning UIs; the game uses the frame's setting reader.\n\n## Local engine patches\n\nNone. All 2,135 engine-owned files remain byte-identical, verified by \"'`node x engine`.\nEOF\nnpx prettier --write labs/game/audio/sound.test.ts labs/game/tools/record-replays.ts > out/game/format-audio.log\nnpm run check > out/game/check.log 2>&1'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_120","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '45,120p' engine/input/devices/keyboard.ts; sed -n '33,94p' labs/game/ui/shell.ts; sed -n '115,160p' labs/game/ui/shell.ts; sed -n '1,80p' labs/game/main.ts; sed -n '70,90p' engine/ui/overlay.ts; sed -n '1,115p' engine/input/devices/gamepad.ts\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_120","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '45,120p' engine/input/devices/keyboard.ts; sed -n '33,94p' labs/game/ui/shell.ts; sed -n '115,160p' labs/game/ui/shell.ts; sed -n '1,80p' labs/game/main.ts; sed -n '70,90p' engine/ui/overlay.ts; sed -n '1,115p' engine/input/devices/gamepad.ts\"","aggregated_output":"  const down = (event: Event) => {\n    const { code, repeat } = event as KeyEventLike;\n    if (!code || deviceOf(code) !== 'keyboard' || isTyping(event.target)) return;\n    if (sink.bound(code)) event.preventDefault();\n    if (!repeat) sink.press(code, 'keyboard');\n  };\n  const up = (event: Event) => {\n    const { code } = event as KeyEventLike;\n    if (code) sink.release(code);\n  };\n  target.addEventListener('keydown', down);\n  target.addEventListener('keyup', up);\n  return () => {\n    target.removeEventListener('keydown', down);\n    target.removeEventListener('keyup', up);\n  };\n}\n      if (this.note('keyboard')) {\n        event.preventDefault();\n        return;\n      }\n      if (!this.choices.length) return;\n      if (['ArrowUp', 'ArrowDown', 'ArrowLeft', 'ArrowRight', 'Enter', 'Space', 'Escape', 'Tab'].includes(event.code))\n        event.preventDefault();\n      if (event.repeat && ['Enter', 'Space', 'Escape'].includes(event.code)) return;\n      if (event.code === 'ArrowUp') this.move(-1);\n      if (event.code === 'ArrowDown' || event.code === 'Tab') this.move(1);\n      if (event.code === 'ArrowLeft') this.adjust(-1);\n      if (event.code === 'ArrowRight') this.adjust(1);\n      if ((event.code === 'Enter' || event.code === 'Space') && !(event.target instanceof HTMLInputElement))\n        this.pick();\n      if (event.code === 'Escape') this.back();\n    });\n    window.addEventListener('pointermove', (event) => {\n      if (event.pointerType !== 'touch' && (event.movementX || event.movementY)) this.note('mouse');\n    });\n    window.addEventListener('pointerdown', (event) => {\n      if (event.pointerType !== 'touch') this.note('mouse');\n      else this.lastInput = performance.now();\n    });\n  }\n  note(device: Device): boolean {\n    const changed = this.device !== device;\n    this.device = device;\n    this.lastInput = performance.now();\n    const consumed = this.interaction() === true;\n    if (changed)\n      for (const parent of [this.root, this.hud, this.banner])\n        parent.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-glyph]').forEach((node) => {\n          node.outerHTML = glyph(node.dataset.glyph ?? 'accept', device, this.xbox);\n        });\n    return consumed;\n  }\n  menu(\n    screen: string,\n    eyebrow: string,\n    title: string,\n    description: string,\n    choices: Choice[],\n    options: { extra?: string; footer?: string; hero?: boolean; wide?: boolean } = {},\n  ): void {\n    const prior = this.screen === screen ? this.focus : 0;\n    this.screen = screen;\n    this.choices = choices;\n    this.focus = 0;\n    this.root.className = `screen screen-${screen}${options.hero ? ' hero-screen' : ''}${options.wide ? ' wide-screen' : ''}`;\n    this.root.innerHTML = `<div class=\"paper-wash\"></div><div class=\"masthead\"><span class=\"leaf\">${LEAF}</span><span>LITTLE FULCRUM<span class=\"masthead-small\">WELLNESS RETREAT</span></span><span class=\"edition\">EST. APPROXIMATELY LEVEL</span></div><main class=\"menu-panel\"><div class=\"eyebrow\"><span class=\"tiny-line\"></span>${safe(eyebrow)}</div><h1>${title}</h1>${description ? `<p class=\"description\">${safe(description)}</p>` : ''}${options.extra ?? ''}<div class=\"menu-list\" role=\"menu\" aria-label=\"${safe(screen)}\">${choices.map((choice, i) => `<button type=\"button\" data-choice=\"${i}\" data-action=\"${safe(choice.id)}\" role=\"menuitem\" class=\"menu-choice${i === 0 ? ' focused' : ''}\" tabindex=\"${i === 0 ? '0' : '-1'}\"><span class=\"choice-number\">${String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span><span class=\"choice-content\"><span class=\"choice-label\">${safe(choice.label)}</span>${choice.detail ? `<span class=\"choice-detail\">${safe(choice.detail)}</span>` : ''}</span><span class=\"choice-value\">${safe(choice.value ?? '')}</span><span class=\"choice-arrow\">↗</span></button>${choice.slider ? `<input aria-label=\"${safe(choice.label)}\" data-slider=\"${i}\" type=\"range\" min=\"${choice.slider.min}\" max=\"${choice.slider.max}\" step=\"${choice.slider.step}\" value=\"${choice.slider.value}\">` : ''}`).join('')}</div></main><footer class=\"screen-footer\"><span>${options.footer ?? `${glyph('accept', this.device, this.xbox)} Select <span class=\"footer-dot\">·</span> ${glyph('back', this.device, this.xbox)} Back`}</span><span class=\"footer-right\">A LITTLE PRACTICE. A LITTLE LESS WOBBLE.</span></footer>`;\n    this.root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-choice]').forEach((button) => {\n      const index = Number(button.dataset.choice);\n      button.addEventListener('pointerenter', () => this.setFocus(index));\n      button.addEventListener('click', () => {\n        this.setFocus(index);\n        this.pick();\n      });\n    });\n    this.setFocus(prior);\n    this.root.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('[data-slider]').forEach((slider) =>\n      slider.addEventListener('input', () => {\n        this.setFocus(Number(slider.dataset.slider));\n    if (this.choices.length) this.setFocus((this.focus + direction + this.choices.length) % this.choices.length);\n  }\n  adjust(direction: number): void {\n    this.choices[this.focus]?.adjust?.(direction);\n  }\n  pick(): void {\n    this.choices[this.focus]?.action();\n  }\n  updatePad(dt: number): void {\n    const pads = navigator.getGamepads?.() ?? [];\n    const pad = [...pads].find((p) => p?.connected);\n    if (!pad) return;\n    const b = pad.buttons.map((x) => x.pressed),\n      active = b.some(Boolean) || pad.axes.some((a) => Math.abs(a) > 0.3);\n    if (active && this.note('pad')) {\n      this.padOld = b;\n      return;\n    }\n    const press = (n: number) => b[n] && !this.padOld[n];\n    this.padRepeat = Math.max(0, this.padRepeat - dt);\n    if (this.choices.length) {\n      if ((b[12] || pad.axes[1] < -0.5) && this.padRepeat === 0) {\n        this.move(-1);\n        this.padRepeat = 0.2;\n      }\n      if ((b[13] || pad.axes[1] > 0.5) && this.padRepeat === 0) {\n        this.move(1);\n        this.padRepeat = 0.2;\n      }\n      if ((b[14] || pad.axes[0] < -0.5) && this.padRepeat === 0) {\n        this.adjust(-1);\n        this.padRepeat = 0.1;\n      }\n      if ((b[15] || pad.axes[0] > 0.5) && this.padRepeat === 0) {\n        this.adjust(1);\n        this.padRepeat = 0.1;\n      }\n      if (press(0)) this.pick();\n      if (press(1)) this.back();\n    }\n    this.padOld = b;\n  }\n}\n/** @file Boots the self-contained retreat on the read-only my-3dge runtime. */\nimport { createEngine } from '../../engine';\nimport { GameApp } from './app';\nimport { startSound } from './audio/sound';\nimport { HubSession } from './hub/session';\nimport { island, round } from './scenes/island';\nimport { SHOT } from './cameras/retreat';\nimport type { GameEngine } from './ui/context';\nimport './looks/retreat';\nimport './bodies/retreat';\nimport './ui/input';\nimport './ui/theme.css';\nconst app = new GameApp(startSound());\nconst session = new HubSession(app);\nawait session.connect();\nconst search = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\nfor (const key of [...search.keys()]) if (key.startsWith('aihub')) search.delete(key);\nsearch.set('touch', 'off');\nsearch.set('cam3', 'retreat');\nsearch.set('post.look', 'look:retreat');\nsearch.set('gfx.resolution', 'full');\nsearch.set('quality', 'high');\nsearch.set('gfx.governor', 'false');\nif (session.info) {\n  search.set('scene', round.id);\n  search.set('seed', String(session.info.seed));\n}\nif (!('gpu' in navigator)) {\n  document.querySelector('#msg')?.setAttribute('hidden', '');\n  app.noGpu = true;\n  app.show('title');\n  if (session.info) session.client?.fail('WebGPU required');\n} else {\n  const watchdog = session.info ? setTimeout(() => session.client?.ready(), 14000) : 0;\n  const engine = await createEngine({\n    canvas: document.querySelector<HTMLCanvasElement>('#view')!,\n    scenes: [island.id, round.id],\n    search: `?${search}`,\n    hash: '',\n    store: app.store,\n    actionMap: 'actionMap:menuRetreat',\n    modal: () => app.ui.choices.length > 0 || app.ui.screen === 'hub',\n    cameraInput: () => ({ follow: SHOT.feet as [number, number, number] }),\n    onFrame: (frame) => {\n      app.frame(frame);\n      session.frame();\n    },\n  });\n  if (watchdog) clearTimeout(watchdog);\n  app.attach(engine as GameEngine);\n  if (engine.ready) {\n    document.querySelector('#msg')?.setAttribute('hidden', '');\n    session.ready();\n  } else if (session.info) session.client?.fail('WebGPU required');\n}\n  'top-right',\n  'bottom-left',\n  'bottom',\n  'bottom-right',\n];\n\n/** How a HUD line is shown. */\nexport interface HudOptions {\n  /** Its place (`top-left`); lines in one place stack in the order they were first set. */\n  at?: HudPlace;\n  /** A key hint (false): marked `data-keyboard`, so touch screens hide it. */\n  keys?: boolean;\n  /** Its text colour (CSS). */\n  color?: string;\n}\n\n/** How an overlay is made. */\nexport interface OverlayOptions {\n  /** The canvas the game draws on: the overlay covers it, and follows its size and place each frame. */\n  canvas: HTMLCanvasElement;\n}\n/**\n * @file The gamepad device (PLAN.md WP 3.3, I-24): polls the Gamepad API once per sample and writes its buttons and\n * sticks as codes (engine/input/codes.ts). Any slot works: the active pad stays while it is connected, a pad in\n * another slot takes over when it is used while the active one rests, and a pad that leaves (disconnected or\n * replaced) releases everything it held at once.\n *\n * Sticks get a radial deadzone, rescaled so the stick still reaches 1: a lean of l ≤ d gives 0, otherwise the\n * direction times min(1, (l − d) / (1 − d)), so there is no jump at the edge and no drift. The four direction codes of\n * each stick carry how far it leans that way, so a half-pushed stick walks at half speed; they count as held from 0.5\n * and let go below 0.4, as the triggers do (analog, `value` 0 to 1). Other buttons are held as the browser reports.\n *\n * Invariants: buttons are read by the standard mapping's index (`PAD_BUTTONS`); a pad with another `mapping` is read\n * the same way, as browsers expose it. `deadzone` is clamped to [0.05, 0.5]. Nothing here reads a clock.\n *\n * Carried from `my-3d2dge:engine/my-3d2dge.js:595-619` (`tick`: any slot, the radial deadzone, release on\n * disconnect) and `my-3d2dge:docs/CONTROLS-AUDIT.md` (slot 0 only, drift and stuck buttons were its bugs).\n *\n * @example\n * radialDeadzone(0.1, 0, 0.18); // [0, 0]: inside the deadzone\n * radialDeadzone(0.59, 0, 0.18); // [0.5, 0]: rescaled, so half the travel past the deadzone is 0.5\n * radialDeadzone(0, -1, 0.18); // [0, -1]: still reaches the edge\n * @see engine/input/devices/devices.test.ts\n */\nimport { MathUtils } from '../../core/math';\nimport { PAD_BUTTONS, padStyle, type InputSink, type PadStyle } from '../codes';\n\n/** The Gamepad API's `Gamepad`, as far as the device reads it (a test stub gives just this). */\nexport interface GamepadLike {\n  readonly id: string;\n  readonly index: number;\n  readonly connected: boolean;\n  readonly mapping?: string;\n  readonly axes: readonly number[];\n  readonly buttons: readonly { readonly pressed: boolean; readonly value: number }[];\n}\n\n/** Where pads come from: `navigator.getGamepads`, or a test's slots. */\nexport type GamepadSource = () => readonly (GamepadLike | null)[];\n\n/** The stick deadzone by default (the prototype's). */\nexport const DEADZONE = 0.18;\n\n/** An analog code is held from this strength… */\nconst PRESS = 0.5;\n/** …until it falls below this one. */\nconst LET_GO = 0.4;\n\n/** A stick reading with a radial deadzone `d`, rescaled so the edge still reaches 1. */\nexport function radialDeadzone(x: number, y: number, d: number): [number, number] {\n  const length = Math.hypot(x, y);\n  if (length <= d || length === 0) return [0, 0];\n  const k = Math.min(1, (length - d) / (1 - d)) / length;\n  return [x * k, y * k];\n}\n\n/** The gamepad device: `poll()` once per sample; the right stick and the family for the camera and prompts. */\nexport interface GamepadDevice {\n  /** Reads the pads and writes the active one's codes. */\n  poll(): void;\n  /** The active pad's right stick after the deadzone, `[x, y]` with y down as the API gives it; `[0, 0]` without one. */\n  rightStick(): [number, number];\n  /** The active pad's slot, or null. */\n  readonly index: number | null;\n  /** The active pad's family, for labels. */\n  readonly style: PadStyle;\n  /** Lets go of the active pad (a `gamepaddisconnected`, or a page blur). */\n  release(): void;\n}\n\n/** Makes the gamepad device over `source`, writing to `sink`. */\nexport function createGamepadDevice(sink: InputSink, source: GamepadSource, deadzone = DEADZONE): GamepadDevice {\n  const d = MathUtils.clamp(deadzone, 0.05, 0.5);\n  let active: { index: number; id: string } | null = null;\n  let right: [number, number] = [0, 0];\n  let style: PadStyle = 'xbox';\n  const held = new Set<string>();\n  const set = (code: string, value: number, down: boolean) => {\n    if (down && !held.has(code)) {\n      held.add(code);\n      sink.press(code, 'gamepad');\n    } else if (!down && held.delete(code)) sink.release(code);\n    sink.analog(code, value);\n  };\n  const busy = (pad: GamepadLike) =>\n    pad.buttons.some((button) => button.pressed) ||\n    Math.hypot(pad.axes[0] ?? 0, pad.axes[1] ?? 0) > d ||\n    Math.hypot(pad.axes[2] ?? 0, pad.axes[3] ?? 0) > d;\n  const device: GamepadDevice = {\n    get index() {\n      return active?.index ?? null;\n    },\n    get style() {\n      return style;\n    },\n    rightStick: () => [...right],\n    release() {\n      for (const code of held) sink.release(code);\n      held.clear();\n      right = [0, 0];\n      active = null;\n    },\n    poll() {\n      let pads: GamepadLike[] = [];\n      try {\n        pads = [...source()].filter((pad): pad is GamepadLike => !!pad && pad.connected !== false);\n      } catch {\n        pads = []; // a page in a frame may not read gamepads\n      }\n      let pad = pads.find((p) => active && p.index === active.index && p.id === active.id);\n      const other = pads.find((p) => p !== pad && busy(p));\n      if (!pad || (other && !busy(pad))) {\n        if (active) device.release();\n        pad = other ?? pads[0];\n        if (!pad) return;\n        active = { index: pad.index, id: pad.id };\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_121","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > labs/game/tools/flow-debug.py <<'EOF'\n# @file Focused input-flow diagnosis, independent of visual timing.\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\nwith sync_playwright() as p:\n b=p.chromium.launch(args=['--no-sandbox','--enable-unsafe-webgpu','--enable-features=Vulkan','--use-vulkan=swiftshader','--use-angle=swiftshader'])\n page=b.new_page(viewport={'width':1280,'height':720})\n page.add_init_script(\\\"window.__pad={id:'DualSense',index:0,connected:true,mapping:'standard',axes:[0,0,0,0],buttons:Array.from({length:17},()=>({pressed:false,value:0}))};navigator.getGamepads=()=>[window.__pad]\\\")\n page.on('pageerror',lambda e:print('ERROR',e,flush=True))\n page.goto((Path.cwd().parent/'Wobble-Fit-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261104-224022.html').as_uri())\n page.wait_for_function('__engine.ready',timeout=90000)\n def dump(label): print(label,json.dumps(page.evaluate('({game:__game,heading:document.querySelector(\\\"#shell h1\\\")?.innerText,errors:__engine.errors})')),flush=True)\n dump('boot')\n for key in ['Enter','ArrowDown','ArrowDown','Enter','Enter','Escape']:\n  page.keyboard.press(key);page.wait_for_timeout(750);dump(key)\n page.evaluate('__pad.buttons[13]={pressed:true,value:1}');page.wait_for_timeout(600);dump('pad')\n b.close()\nEOF\npython3 -u labs/game/tools/flow-debug.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
