{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_154","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > labs/game/tools/export-report.ts <<'EOF'\n/** @file Exports the exact canonical in-game report for the game importer. */\nimport {writeFileSync} from 'node:fs';\nimport {REPORT} from '../ui/about-data';\nwriteFileSync('../exit-interview.json',JSON.stringify(REPORT,null,2)+'\\\\n');\nEOF\ncat > labs/game/tools/verify.mjs <<'EOF'\n/** @file One quiet verification entry: objective suites, cross-runtime replays, browser input and the real Hub harness. */\nimport {spawnSync} from 'node:child_process';\nimport {mkdirSync,readFileSync,writeFileSync,existsSync} from 'node:fs';\nimport {createHash} from 'node:crypto';\nimport {resolve} from 'node:path';\nconst dir=resolve('out/verify');mkdirSync(dir,{recursive:true});\nlet passed=0,failed=0;\nconst json=(path)=>JSON.parse(readFileSync(path,'utf8'));\nfunction run(name,command,args,count){\n const result=spawnSync(command,args,{encoding:'utf8',timeout:600000,env:{...process.env,PLAYWRIGHT_HOST_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE:'ubuntu24.04-x64',CHROMIUM_PATH:process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH??'/home/micha/.cache/ms-playwright/chromium_headless_shell-1243/chrome-headless-shell-linux64/chrome-headless-shell'},maxBuffer:32*1024*1024});\n const output=(result.stdout??'')+(result.stderr??'');writeFileSync(\"'`${dir}/${name}.log`,output);\n if(result.status!==0){failed++;console.log(`FAIL ${name}'\"\\\\n\"'${output.trim()}`);return false;}\n passed+=typeof count==='\"'function'?count():count;return true;\n}\nrun('static','npm',['run','check'],4);\nrun('simulation-audio','npm',['test','--','--maxWorkers=1'],()=>json('out/test/report.json').numPassedTests);\nrun('cross-runtime','node',['x','replay','labs/game/replays','--browser','sim','--runs','2'],14);\nrun('metadata','node',['--import','tsx','labs/game/tools/export-report.ts'],1);\ntry{\n const file='../Wobble-Fit-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261104-224022.html',html=readFileSync(file,'utf8');\n const client=readFileSync('labs/game/hub/session-client.txt','utf8');\n const hash=createHash('sha256').update(client.trimEnd()).digest('hex');\n if(hash\"'!=='\"'529eac78c54cfff0e60d375a9c63f66d1a594327ddcc262a2bdf9b1f2fb6582a'||\"'!html.includes(client))throw Error('\"'The Hub client differs from its unmodified source.');\n if(/<script[\"'^>]+src=|<link[''^>]+rel=\"stylesheet\"/.test(html))throw Error('\"'The build has an external script or style.');\n if(/data:audio\\\\//.test(html))throw Error('The build contains an audio recording.');\n const report=json('../exit-interview.json');if(report.sourceInformation.usage\"'!=='\"'added on import'||report.aiHub.name\"'!=='\"'Wobble Fit')throw Error('Exit interview fields do not match the game.');\n passed+=4;\n}catch(error){failed++;console.log(\"'`FAIL package: ${error.message}`);}\nif(!process.argv.includes('\"'--quick')){\n run('browser','python3',['-u','labs/game/tools/browser-check.py'],()=>json('out/game/browser-report.json').passed);\n run('hub','python3',['-u','labs/game/tools/hub-check.py'],()=>json('out/game/hub-report.json').passed);\n if(existsSync('labs/game/tools/viewport-check.py'))run('viewport','python3',['-u','labs/game/tools/viewport-check.py'],()=>json('out/game/viewport-report.json').passed);\n}\nwriteFileSync(\"'`${dir}/report.json`,JSON.stringify({passed,failed},null,2)+'\"'\\\\n');\nconsole.log(\"'`${passed} checks passed; ${failed} failed`);process.exitCode=failed?1:0;\nEOF\ncat >> ../PROGRESS.md <<'\"'EOF'\n\n## Midnight integration update (Nov 5)\n- Simulation + numerical audio suite: 19/19 passed. Four full story runs were not claimed; the actual test uses 3 seeds, all five days and credits.\n- First 14 golden replays passed Node ×2 and Chromium ×2. They now need re-recording because final content added fields/remarks, not because determinism diverged.\n- \"'`npm run check` passed all 4 tool families before the final UI/session changes; engine remains read-only.\n- Strong Hub tests correctly rejected a protocol-only success while WebGPU was still warming. `gfx.warmUp=asked`, a small session look, seat-coloured bodies prepared at spawn, and session-only reduced shadow work make the actual scene ready. A 2-player harness now passes with ready=true, no engine errors and real ghost entities.\n- Found and fixed an important input integration issue: a fixed `EngineOptions.actionMap` resets `input.use` every sample. The page now supplies a single reactive map function, also used by its menus.\n- Found and fixed rejected ghost arrays: scene actions require an object; list payloads are wrapped in `{items}`.\n- The renderer cannot gate menu/controller polling. UI uses an independent 16 ms timer; pad input while paused is now observable.\n- `GPUShaderStage` is read by three.js at module import even in unsupported Firefox. The HTML provides only the standard enum constants, without pretending a GPU exists; actual capability is still probed, and unsupported browsers show a friendly page.\n- Native touch layer is removed after engine attachment in addition to touch=off, so no hidden touch-control DOM remains.\n- Latest built HTML includes these changes. Current running session 83090 is browser-check.py; read out/game/browser.log for its failures/status. Do not build over the HTML while a test starts new pages.\n- Last Hub quick run passed 1/1. Full 2/3/4/host-leave still required. No server is left running between scripts; each harness owns and closes its ephemeral server.\n- Remaining finish: final browser checks, full Hub, viewport matrix + inspect screenshots, finalize feedback counts, generate exit-interview.json, record final goldens, run one-command verify, update progress complete, deliver root HTML and reports.\n- One-command verifier and report exporter are now in labs/game/tools/. The viewport script has not yet been written.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
