{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_209","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('labs/game/props/retreat.ts');s=p.read_text();s=s.replace('const builders:', \\\"const makePondSurface=()=>defineProp('prop:pondSurface',{description:'The still water under the frog\\\\'s jetty.',parts:[{name:'water',geometry:'geometry:box',params:{width:19,height:.025,depth:18},material:'material:retreatSea',shadow:false}]});\\\\nconst builders:\\\")\ns=s.replace('sea: makeSea,', 'sea:makeSea,pondSurface:makePondSurface,')\n# Keep the descriptive string plain and unambiguous after the source insertion.\ns=s.replace(\\\"description:'The still water under the frog's jetty.'\\\", \\\"description:'The still water under the jetty.'\\\")\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('labs/game/scenes/world.ts');s=p.read_text().replace(\\\"  put(w, 'pier', -70, -12, 4);\\\", \\\"  put(w,'pondSurface',-70,-12,4.01);\\\\n  put(w, 'pier', -70, -12, 4);\\\")\np.write_text(s)\np=Path('labs/game/tools/scope-props.mjs')\nif p.exists():p.unlink()\np=Path('labs/game/ui/about-data.ts');s=p.read_text().replace('32 distinct issues', '34 distinct issues').replace('Add a first-class multi-seat input API that remains usable while the simulation is paused.', 'Expose scene-scoped prop warm-up so unplaced island assets do not load in a small session scene.')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ncat >> labs/game/scenes/game.test.ts <<'EOF'\n\nit('terraces and physical mats support the complete body above the visible floor',async()=>{\n expect(heightAt(-57.4,20)).toBe(8);expect(heightAt(0,34)).toBe(8);expect(heightAt(30,-48)).toBe(11);expect(heightAt(-70,-12)).toBe(4);expect(heightAt(0,0)).toBe(18);\n const h=await createHeadless({scene:island,seed:53}) as GameInspector;h.step(120);const actor=h.get(flow(h).hero)?.actor as {y:number};expect(actor.y).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(8);expect(actor.y).toBeLessThan(8.4);expect(h.errors).toHaveLength(0);\n});\nEOF\ncat >> ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md <<'EOF'\n\nThe most important late finding was prop warm-up scope. \"'`createPropMeshes` prepares every registered prop, including unplaced ones. Importing the complete retreat library therefore made the small session scene warm the entire island'\"'s geometry. The game now registers prop factories at scene setup: only mats, pavilion and guide in a session, the complete library on the island. The engine is unchanged. A public scene-scoped prop list would remove this workaround and make the small-scene deadline reliable.\n\nTerrain flats are heights above the terrain origin, not absolute elevations. The origin was -1 m, leaving the characters one metre below the decorative terraces. The game offsets its flat specs and supplies physical mat, platform and jetty supports. A regression checks the actual supported feet height.\nEOF\ncat >> labs/game/README.md <<'EOF'\n\nProp definitions are registered by \"'`registerRetreat(small)` during scene setup. The renderer prewarms every registered prop; keeping the island-only definitions out of the session registry avoids compiling unplaced island geometry. A running island (or headless `createHeadless({scene:island})`) registers the complete library for inspection. The text factories remain normal native prop definitions.\nEOF\nnpx prettier --write labs/game > out/game/format-final.log\nnpx tsc -b tsconfig.check.json --pretty false\nnpm test -- --maxWorkers=1 > out/game/tests.log 2>&1'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
