{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_235","type":"agent_message","text":"Built [**Wobble Fit**](</home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261104-224022__x54facc/work/Wobble-Fit-Wii-Fit-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261104-224022.html>): five days, 13 activities, the storm finale, local multiplayer and AI Hub ghosts. Open the offline HTML in Chrome or Edge with WebGPU.\n\n**Validation:** 101 checks passed, zero failures. All 2,135 engine files remain unchanged.\n\n[Exit interview](</home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261104-224022__x54facc/work/exit-interview.json>) · [Completed progress record](</home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/gpt-6.1-sol-max.build-v2__20261104-224022__x54facc/work/PROGRESS.md>)\n\n**Source Information:** Date: 2026-11-04 22:40:22. Source: Wii Fit. Plan: PLAN.md. Genre: 3D sports/wellness anthology with exploration and comedy. Perspective: third person with activity cameras. Tech: [my-3dge e7a1243](https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3dge/tree/e7a124394afe087a40c36e2662a5c4ca2b39a663), TypeScript 5.9.3, three.js r182/WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite 7.3.7 and Vitest 4.1.12.\n\nArt: native toon puppets and original procedural retreat assets. Animation: native clip layers, original input-scrubbed poses and Mesh2Motion reference rest. Audio: eight coded tracker songs, synthesized effects and gibberish voices; music defaults to 10%. Online: [AI Hub v1 ghost sessions](https://github.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/blob/main/lib/hub/README.md) and local 1–4-player Group Class. Research: provided plan, pinned engine and official Hub documentation. Testing: headless simulation, full playthroughs, replays, browser controls and viewport checks. Environment: Codex CLI, headless Linux/WSL2. Model: OpenAI gpt-6.1-sol, reasoning effort max. Usage: **added on import**.\n\n**Testing Feedback:** 34 logged issues corrected; 14 could block play or integration. Most helpful: Hub checks asserting actual engine readiness and ghost entities. Least helpful: fixed browser delays; live-state waits were more reliable. Physical controller feel, real iOS behavior and human audio quality remain unknown.\n\n**Engine Feedback:** Best feature: deterministic headless simulation and procedural assets. Incorrect assumptions involved action-map switching, action arguments and pending entities. The main custom work was balance, activities, poses, local seats and UI. Four-copy startup was hardest. Engine changes: none. Most wanted improvement: scene-scoped prop warm-up.\n\n**Prompt Feedback:** The shared balance verb and growing island story worked well. Some tested API examples needed adjustment. Combining the complete residency, offline packaging and multiplayer startup was hardest. I would provide a generated pinned workspace and machine-readable acceptance checklist."}}
